1
00:00:14,550 --> 00:00:18,950
August 2017. For four days, a
hurricane's rain falls on Houston,

2
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:21,791
the fourth-largest city in America.

3
00:00:22,541 --> 00:00:25,701
Across Texas, more than
a hundred and twenty-two

4
00:00:25,741 --> 00:00:27,536
thousand people will have to be rescued.

5
00:00:29,086 --> 00:00:32,406
The flood was forecast, days in advance.

6
00:00:33,056 --> 00:00:36,482
So why did so many people end
up waiting on their roofs?

7
00:00:46,632 --> 00:00:49,192
Friday, August twenty-fifth.

8
00:00:49,232 --> 00:00:53,432
Two days ago, Harvey came back
to life over the Gulf of Mexico.

9
00:00:53,472 --> 00:00:56,965
Now it is growing fast, and
it is heading for Texas.

10
00:00:57,715 --> 00:00:59,595
At four in the afternoon,
the National Hurricane

11
00:00:59,635 --> 00:01:02,695
Center warns of catastrophic,
life-threatening flooding.

12
00:01:02,735 --> 00:01:07,918
Fifteen to thirty inches
of rain. In places, forty.

13
00:01:09,068 --> 00:01:14,177
The warning is clear. What no forecast
can show is which streets will flood.

14
00:01:15,927 --> 00:01:19,567
Along the coast, counties
order people to leave.

15
00:01:19,607 --> 00:01:21,577
Houston and Harris County do not.

16
00:01:22,077 --> 00:01:23,637
County Judge Ed Emmett explains why.

17
00:01:23,677 --> 00:01:26,997
With a storm surge, you
know who lives in its path.

18
00:01:27,037 --> 00:01:30,983
With rain, you don't know which
neighbourhoods will flood.

19
00:01:31,933 --> 00:01:33,886
And Houston remembers Rita.

20
00:01:34,086 --> 00:01:36,986
In 2005, millions tried to
leave the city at once.

21
00:01:37,026 --> 00:01:41,626
Dozens of people died during that
evacuation, twenty-three of them

22
00:01:41,666 --> 00:01:45,803
in one bus fire on the highway,
the day before Rita came ashore.

23
00:01:46,953 --> 00:01:48,833
At about ten on Friday night,

24
00:01:48,873 --> 00:01:52,737
Harvey comes ashore near
Rockport, a Category 4 hurricane.

25
00:01:53,437 --> 00:01:55,022
And then it stops.

26
00:02:01,372 --> 00:02:06,199
Saturday night. Harvey's rain bands
settle over Houston, and stay.

27
00:02:06,599 --> 00:02:11,150
At nine twenty-seven, the weather service
issues its first flash flood emergency.

28
00:02:11,750 --> 00:02:15,482
By two in the morning, five inches
have fallen at Hobby Airport.

29
00:02:15,882 --> 00:02:18,054
By nine, more than eleven.

30
00:02:19,804 --> 00:02:22,084
South-east of the city, in Dickinson,

31
00:02:22,124 --> 00:02:25,484
the water is already inside
Matthew Dusek's house.

32
00:02:25,524 --> 00:02:27,100
He is a Coast Guard chief.

33
00:02:27,650 --> 00:02:31,300
the night that it was happening
it was up to our box spring.

34
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:36,025
When daylight comes,
the highways are rivers.

35
00:02:37,175 --> 00:02:40,211
Cars sit in water up to their windows.

36
00:02:41,161 --> 00:02:46,903
In fifteen hours, Harris County's 911
system takes fifty-six thousand calls.

37
00:02:48,653 --> 00:02:51,331
The county judge goes on
the air with a request.

38
00:02:56,081 --> 00:02:58,001
Early that Sunday, a
Houston police sergeant,

39
00:02:58,041 --> 00:03:00,781
Steve Perez, sets off
for work in the rain.

40
00:03:00,821 --> 00:03:05,835
His wife had asked him not to
go, the police chief said later.

41
00:03:06,235 --> 00:03:10,395
He drowns in his patrol car on
a flooded road in north Houston.

42
00:03:10,435 --> 00:03:12,576
He is not found for two days.

43
00:03:14,126 --> 00:03:16,464
Those who cannot get out go up.

44
00:03:17,014 --> 00:03:19,331
Onto their roofs. And wait.

45
00:03:27,281 --> 00:03:29,201
From as far away as Cape
Cod, Massachusetts,

46
00:03:29,241 --> 00:03:33,042
Coast Guard helicopters
are arriving over Houston.

47
00:03:34,392 --> 00:03:36,252
Most calls are just addresses from 911.

48
00:03:36,292 --> 00:03:42,532
One of the Cape Cod pilots, Simon Greene,
said later that they followed the roads.

49
00:03:42,572 --> 00:03:44,312
The pilot who was not flying typed each

50
00:03:44,352 --> 00:03:47,364
address into a phone,
and called out the turns.

51
00:04:15,014 --> 00:04:18,497
One of the rescue swimmers flying
those calls is Brendan Kiley.

52
00:04:19,447 --> 00:04:22,587
On his second day in Houston, he
is lowered to a one-story house.

53
00:04:22,627 --> 00:04:25,187
Five people are waiting on the roof.

54
00:04:25,227 --> 00:04:29,417
The water is almost over
the top of a car beside it.

55
00:04:29,802 --> 00:04:32,542
A woman pushes a big plastic
storage bin toward him.

56
00:04:32,582 --> 00:04:37,964
He thinks it is luggage, and tells her
there is no room for it. She pushes it back.

57
00:04:38,664 --> 00:04:39,744
Inside are her two children.

58
00:04:39,784 --> 00:04:43,081
A toddler, holding a newborn baby.

59
00:04:44,281 --> 00:04:47,701
He carries the bin down first,
with the children inside.

60
00:04:47,741 --> 00:04:49,781
Then he helps their mother down.

61
00:04:49,821 --> 00:04:52,562
The basket goes up with
all three of them together.

62
00:04:53,912 --> 00:04:58,128
Over three days, Kiley's crew
rescues a hundred and twelve people.

63
00:04:58,528 --> 00:05:03,348
When the heaviest rain bands come through,
Greene said, the pilots cannot see.

64
00:05:03,388 --> 00:05:05,408
They set down in a
ballpark or a parking lot,

65
00:05:05,448 --> 00:05:08,538
wait for the band to
pass, and lift off again.

66
00:05:09,474 --> 00:05:11,514
On the ground, Harris
County's firefighters and

67
00:05:11,554 --> 00:05:15,974
police record more than
sixty-one thousand rescues.

68
00:05:16,014 --> 00:05:18,809
No one counts the people saved by
neighbours in their own boats.

69
00:05:19,959 --> 00:05:21,979
Army National Guard trucks
drive into the water.

70
00:05:22,019 --> 00:05:25,947
Sergeant Anthony Lara's first
mission is in Dickinson.

71
00:05:26,047 --> 00:05:28,567
and it got too deep to go in.

72
00:05:28,607 --> 00:05:34,417
But we were able to rescue some civilians
that did come up to us with civilians.

73
00:05:35,147 --> 00:05:37,747
In League City, Specialist
Kyle Wampler's unit

74
00:05:37,787 --> 00:05:40,654
pulls out an elderly
man who can barely walk.

75
00:05:40,754 --> 00:05:43,394
really stood out to me because I know
that if we weren't there to help them

76
00:05:43,434 --> 00:05:45,724
that you know I don't know
who else would or could.

77
00:05:46,704 --> 00:05:49,044
On Tuesday, a New York
Air National Guard crew

78
00:05:49,084 --> 00:05:51,917
lifts a family out of a
flooded neighbourhood.

79
00:06:03,667 --> 00:06:08,135
West of downtown, a different danger
is building, behind two dams.

80
00:06:08,535 --> 00:06:11,095
Addicks and Barker were
built in the 1940s to

81
00:06:11,135 --> 00:06:13,515
hold floodwater back before
it reaches the city.

82
00:06:13,555 --> 00:06:19,349
On August twenty-fifth, as planned, the
Army Corps of Engineers closes their gates.

83
00:06:21,099 --> 00:06:21,619
The basins fill.

84
00:06:21,659 --> 00:06:26,279
And inside them, on private land,
whole neighbourhoods have been built.

85
00:06:26,319 --> 00:06:30,259
More than nine thousand homes
and businesses there flood,

86
00:06:30,299 --> 00:06:32,335
from water that is being held back.

87
00:06:33,485 --> 00:06:36,185
Downstream, Buffalo Bayou
is already running high.

88
00:06:36,225 --> 00:06:39,245
Around midnight on August twenty-eighth,

89
00:06:39,285 --> 00:06:43,362
with the pools still rising, the
Corps starts releasing water.

90
00:06:44,712 --> 00:06:46,392
The reason is the safety of the dams.

91
00:06:46,432 --> 00:06:49,112
The government had
estimated that a dam failure

92
00:06:49,152 --> 00:06:52,335
would put six hundred
thousand lives at stake.

93
00:06:54,085 --> 00:06:58,385
The releases flood about four
thousand more homes along the bayou.

94
00:06:58,425 --> 00:07:02,668
On August thirtieth, both reservoirs
reach their highest levels on record.

95
00:07:03,818 --> 00:07:07,498
Years later, federal courts rule that by
flooding these homes to protect others,

96
00:07:07,538 --> 00:07:11,568
the government took private
property, and must pay for it.

97
00:07:11,943 --> 00:07:15,743
One court also praises the Corps'
professionalism, and finds that at the

98
00:07:15,783 --> 00:07:20,001
levels the water actually reached,
the risk of a dam failure was minimal.

99
00:07:24,951 --> 00:07:26,211
Harvey finally drifts east.

100
00:07:26,251 --> 00:07:30,031
Its heaviest rain of all falls
near Beaumont and Port Arthur.

101
00:07:30,071 --> 00:07:34,623
One gauge near Nederland
records more than sixty inches.

102
00:07:42,173 --> 00:07:46,233
Near Beaumont, an Air Force Reserve crew
lowers a pararescueman to a flooded house.

103
00:07:46,273 --> 00:07:49,922
He comes back up with an
older woman in the basket.

104
00:07:51,272 --> 00:07:53,392
In Vidor, a pararescue
team from the Alaska

105
00:07:53,432 --> 00:07:56,656
Air National Guard works
the streets by boat.

106
00:07:56,756 --> 00:08:00,856
Many times past the windows, we've
seen cars completely submerge.

107
00:08:00,896 --> 00:08:02,196
These people need a way out.

108
00:08:02,856 --> 00:08:07,711
In Orange, near the Louisiana line,
people walk out along flooded roads.

109
00:08:08,861 --> 00:08:13,133
West of Houston, the water is still
rising after the rain has stopped.

110
00:08:13,433 --> 00:08:15,953
The Brazos River at Richmond
crests on September first,

111
00:08:15,993 --> 00:08:18,533
more than ten feet above flood stage.

112
00:08:18,573 --> 00:08:23,840
More than two hundred thousand people
are under an evacuation order.

113
00:08:25,190 --> 00:08:29,030
In Pecan Grove, Army National Guard
trucks and a Texas search-and-rescue

114
00:08:29,070 --> 00:08:33,344
team take people out, with their
children, their bags and their dogs.

115
00:08:46,694 --> 00:08:48,474
When the water goes down, everything that

116
00:08:48,514 --> 00:08:51,264
was inside the houses
comes out to the kerb.

117
00:08:52,614 --> 00:08:57,037
In Dickinson, Matthew Dusek has just
talked to his insurance adjuster.

118
00:08:57,137 --> 00:09:00,857
I just talked to the claims adjuster
and it kind of sent me into a little

119
00:09:00,897 --> 00:09:07,527
spin because I don't have a house,
I'm homeless, I don't know.

120
00:09:08,687 --> 00:09:11,267
By the end, more than a hundred
rain gauges have recorded

121
00:09:11,307 --> 00:09:15,907
forty inches or more: the very
top of what was forecast.

122
00:09:17,457 --> 00:09:22,405
Harvey kills sixty-eight people directly,
thirty-six of them in Harris County.

123
00:09:23,005 --> 00:09:27,102
In the county, more than a hundred
and fifty thousand houses flood.

124
00:09:28,602 --> 00:09:31,522
I got my family and I got
my Coast Guard family.

125
00:09:31,562 --> 00:09:33,022
I got my uniform family.

126
00:09:33,062 --> 00:09:35,792
So that's why I hold on to.

127
00:09:37,312 --> 00:09:38,964
The flood was forecast.

128
00:09:39,264 --> 00:09:40,844
But no forecast could name the streets,

129
00:09:40,884 --> 00:09:43,424
and there was no general
order to leave Houston.

130
00:09:43,464 --> 00:09:49,312
When the downpour came on Saturday night,
many people could only wait to be rescued.

131
00:09:50,862 --> 00:09:54,432
On one of those roofs, a mother
had already done what she could.

132
00:09:54,832 --> 00:09:57,112
She put her two children in a plastic bin,

133
00:09:57,152 --> 00:10:00,449
and kept them dry, until
Brendan Kiley reached them.

